Data type   -> What kind of value can this column store?
Constraint  -> What rules must that value obey?
SQL command -> What operation are we asking MySQL to perform?

For exampleki : price DECIMAL(10, 2) NOT NULL DEFAULT 0.00
Break it apart:
price             -> Column name
DECIMAL(10, 2)   -> Data type
NOT NULL         -> Nullability rule
DEFAULT 0.00     -> Default-value rule -- NOT NULL, PRIMARY KEY, UNIQUE, and FOREIGN KEY are not data types

SQL Commands
│
├── DDL — Data Definition Language
│   ├── CREATE
│   ├── ALTER
│   ├── RENAME
│   ├── TRUNCATE
│   └── DROP
│
├── DML — Data Manipulation Language
│   ├── INSERT
│   ├── UPDATE
│   └── DELETE
│
├── DQL — Data Query Language
│   └── SELECT
│
├── TCL — Transaction Control Language
│   ├── START TRANSACTION
│   ├── COMMIT
│   ├── ROLLBACK
│   ├── SAVEPOINT
│   └── ROLLBACK TO SAVEPOINT
│
├── DCL — Data Control Language
│   ├── GRANT
│   └── REVOKE
│
└── Utility / Administration
    ├── USE
    ├── SHOW
    ├── DESCRIBE
    ├── EXPLAIN
